{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/951524-building-a-new-monster","id":951524,"title":"Building a new Monster","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-15T23:49:08-07:00","id":951524,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Building a new Monster","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Unnecessarily antagonistic opening statement. If you don't want to be treated with hostility then don't start by being hostile in your opening line. The group attack against the Promethean forum is not OK. You should avoid using red text as well. Darksider</span><br /> <br /> Right, now that's out of the way, here's some stuff I've been thinking about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> \u200bThere is a force in the universe, an energy, that defies normal definition. It is a force of Creation, Dynamism, and Change. Under certain circumstances, this force will respond to those who are Devout, Obsessed, or otherwise fixated. This force can be channeled into a dead body, or the likeness of a person, imbuing it with new life. Beings thusly animated, and the ones who make them, are...<i> changed</i> by the process. Sometimes physically, sometime mentally, sometimes spiritually. A little energy stays behind in those who channel it. and becomes an integral part of those who are animated by it. They feel compelled to seek answers about this force, and the Supernatural in general.<br /> <br /> That's what I'm willing to start with. It's late and I'm tired. What kind of game would YOU have made, based on the same set of inspirations that Onyx Path used?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 08-16-2016, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T00:30:06-07:00","id":951530,"title":"","content":"I don't really have something to add here in terms of original ideas, but there are a few potential bits of inspiration I can point out.<br /> <br /> First, there's <b>Kindred of the East</b>. It was an Old World of Darkness take on playing as eastern vampires. Simply put, you died and a part of your soul got sent to Hell while your body was still fresh. However, Hell isn't exactly the best guarded place, and your lower soul, aka the P'o, managed to return to the Hun, the higher soul, that remained in your body. You come back to life, can feed from the Chi of other people. Perhaps the only problem is how the Kuei-Jinn (what they're known as) literally require Dharmas (kinda like Humanity) to function. However, a Dharma can be completely different from Humanity, the only similarity that remains with Promethean is that most Kuei-Jinn feel the need for an ascension through the Dharma. For example, following the Devil Tigers is a Dharma based on enlightenment through pain and violence and you supposedly ascend to demonhood at the end. <br /> <br /> The next were a more fansplatted idea that was never followed up on the Rpg.net forums that might be liked. The idea of playing as a Skeleton or a deceased being. The ideas present seem to suggest that the need for living pleasures was desired, as well as and almost need to hold up a facade of humanity, but without the Promethean aspects of &quot;must need humanity at the end&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?477473-Necro-Let-s-Throw-Out-Ideas-For-the-Next-WoD-Fan-Game&amp;p=11040286#post11040286\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...6#post11040286</a><br /> <br /> Through this link, posts 49-58, then abit more on 72 and 74. <br /> <br /> Now that I think of it to throw out one last bit of inspiration, there was an oWoD fangame called &quot;Zombie: the Coil&quot;. So far, these ideas reminded me abit on how there isn't a nWoD gameline for zombies and this could potentially give some inspiration for your ideas.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/ZombieTheCoil\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph.../ZombieTheCoil</a><br /> <br /> Hopefully this stuff helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T00:57:16-07:00","id":951542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/951524-building-a-new-monster?p=951530#post951530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: